From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:01:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb+LibWebView+WebContent: Tell the embedder about
 navigations

A browser's extensions follow the navigations of a tab's frames: when
one starts, commits, fires DOMContentLoaded, loads, or fails, as
Chrome's webNavigation API reports them. WebDriver BiDi learns of
exactly these, but processes hosting web content only report them during
a BiDi session.

Application::set_navigation_event_handler() gives the embedder each
navigation event as BiDi gets it, named as BiDi names it, with the
navigable it's about: those the browser process emits itself, as a
navigation starts or fails there, and those the processes hosting web
content report. While the embedder has a handler, those processes report
them outside of BiDi sessions too, through the same event sink, and
nothing else of BiDi runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
